The previous parts of Phase-02 established the institutional operator model.

This section converts that model into an implementation blueprint.

It defines exactly what must be implemented within the repository to realize the Operator Environment.

Unlike previous documents, this part is implementation-oriented.

It bridges institutional specification and repository implementation.

2. Mission

Provide the complete implementation blueprint for the Operator Environment while remaining fully aligned with the frozen Stage-00 through Stage-24 Phase-01 specifications.

The blueprint defines:

repository ownership
implementation boundaries
implementation responsibilities
integration strategy
implementation order
3. Implementation Philosophy

The Operator Environment shall extend the COREI Operating Environment.

It shall never create independent operator infrastructure.

Implementation shall:

consume existing platform services
consume existing runtime
consume existing governance
consume existing security
consume existing observability
consume existing continuity

Operator-specific behavior shall remain isolated from platform infrastructure.

4. Repository Ownership

The Operator Environment spans multiple repositories while preserving institutional ownership.

COREI OS Repository

Owns:

operator interaction framework
operator presentation
operator UI components
operator layouts
operator interaction engine
Platform Repository

Owns:

operator managers
operator registries
operator state
operator services
operator contracts
Terminal Repositories

Consume:

operator capabilities
operator context
operator personalization
operator awareness

Terminals never implement independent operator frameworks.

Infrastructure Repository

Provides:

identity
authentication
messaging
persistence
observability
deployment

The Operator Environment consumes infrastructure.

