18. Implementation Constraints

The following constraints apply:

No redesign of Phase-01.
No duplication of platform infrastructure.
Repository ownership shall remain unchanged.
Existing runtime shall be consumed.
Every implementation shall expose explicit contracts.
Every implementation shall participate in governance, observability, security, and continuity.
Business logic remains outside the Operator Environment.
19. Success Criteria

The Operator Environment Implementation Blueprint is complete when:

every implementation responsibility has a defined repository owner
implementation boundaries are explicit
existing COREI repositories are extended rather than replaced
operator functionality is cleanly separated from platform infrastructure
repository implementation can begin without further architectural discussion
future Stage-24 phases consume the Operator Environment rather than implementing independent operator frameworks

The Operator Environment Implementation Blueprint establishes the repository implementation roadmap for all operator-centric functionality in COREI, ensuring that every operator capability is implemented as a governed, reusable, extensible, and institutionally aligned component built upon the Operating Environment foundation established in Phase-01.

